{
  "slug": "codedna",
  "name": "Codedna",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "CodeDNA makes any codebase AI-navigable by embedding architectural context directly in source files. One command annotates every file with exports:,\nused_by:, and rules: — so Claude always knows what a file provides, who depends on it, and what constraints must never be violated.\n\nNo API key required. Uses your existing Claude subscription.\n\nSupports Python, TypeScript, JavaScript, Go, Rust, Java, and Ruby.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 agent**, **4 commands** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Agents** (1): `codedna-reviewer` (CodeDNA compliance reviewer)\n- **Commands** (4): `check` (CodeDNA coverage report — find unannotated files and stale used_by references), `impact` (CodeDNA impact analysis — show the full dependency chain for a file before editing or refactoring), `init` (Annotate all unannotated source files in the project with CodeDNA module headers), `manifest` (CodeDNA architectural map — read all module docstrings and return the full project dependency graph in one pass)\n- **Hooks** (4): `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install codedna@claude-community` from `Larens94/codedna` (`codedna-plugin`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 4
  },
